{"packet_id":"D051-01","doc_id":"D051","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Three months' notice to terminate tenancy at will","requirement":"Either party may terminate a tenancy at will by giving three months' written notice. If rent is payable at intervals of less than three months, notice equal to the payment interval or 30 days, whichever is longer, is sufficient.","key_value":"3 months' notice; or payment interval/30 days, whichever longer","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies at will; no specific property type, unit count, or owner type stated.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 12","quoted_span":"Estates at will may be determined by either party by three months' notice in writing for that purpose given to the other party; and, if the rent reserved is payable at periods of less than three months, the time of such notice shall be sufficient if it is equal to the interval between the days of payment or thirty days, whichever is longer.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D051-01","doc_id":"D051","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fourteen days' notice to quit for nonpayment of rent; right to cure","requirement":"For nonpayment of rent, 14 days' written notice to quit is sufficient. A tenant who has not received a similar notice in the past 12 months may cure within 10 days by paying all rent due. The notice must include notification of this right.","key_value":"14 days' notice; 10 days to cure","coverage_conditions":"Tenant at will who has not received a similar notice within the preceding 12 months.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"If the notice fails to include the required notification, the tenant's time to pay or tender rent is extended to the day the answer is due in a possession action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 12","quoted_span":"In case of neglect or refusal to pay the rent due from a tenant at will, fourteen days' notice to quit, given in writing by the landlord to the tenant, shall be sufficient to determine the tenancy; provided, that the tenancy of a tenant who has not received a similar notice from the landlord within the twelve months next preceding the receipt of such notice shall not be determined if the tenant, within ten days after the receipt thereof, pays or tenders to the landlord, the landlord's attorney, or the person to whom the tenant customarily pays rent, the full amount of any rent due.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
